--- !u!114 &-4645247345864011780
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'You can use <b>light layers</b> to dictate which objects can be affected by a light or a Reflection Probe.


      They can be used to help with selective lighting of certain objects, solve light leaking issues, and control which light is allowed to cast shadows onto other objects.


      Understanding Light Layers is an important part of the lighting workflow.'
--- !u!114 &-4614409464732329048
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Let's see how the Light Layers are activated.\r\n\r\n1. In the <i>Project</i> Window, inside <b>Assets</b> > <b>Settings,</b> select the active HDRP asset, most likely <b>HDRPMediumQuality.</b>\r\n\r\n2. In its <i>Inspector,</i> disable the <b>Lighting</b> > <b>Light layers</b> checkbox.\r\n\r\nWith the Light layers off, notice that the top lamp\u2019s glass surface casts unwanted shadows on its siblings and on the floor.\n\r\n3. Turn the Light layers back on. \n\nNotice how the glass doesn\u2019t cast shadow anymore. In this scenario, the Light Layers are used to force each piece of glass to not receive light from other spotlights on the lamp fixture.\n\r\n<b>Note:</b> By default, Light layers are turned off for new projects.\r"
